          "id": "prt_msg_ses_36_04_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_36",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_36_04",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Right, and it's intentional: `^7.0.0` means \"7.0.0 or anything compatible with it per semver,\" so `7.0.1`, `7.4.0`, `7.5.0` are all fair game, but `8.0.0` is not. `~7.0.0` is tighter — only patch bumps like `7.0.1`, `7.0.2`. No prefix at all, `7.0.0`, means exactly that version and nothing else installs in its place."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_36_04_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_36",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_36_04",
          "type": "step-finish",
