          "id": "prt_msg_ses_36_06_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_36",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_36_06",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That's backwards — under semver it's the *major* number that's explicitly allowed to break compatibility; minor adds features without breaking anything, patch is bugfixes only. A `6.x` → `7.0.0` bump is exactly the signal that something incompatible changed. Worth checking mongoose's changelog/migration guide for v7 before assuming your existing code still works against it."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_36_06_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_36",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_36_06",
